#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046673} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413298} :activity/id #uuid "4e1d8ee8-9c39-5df9-b4e1-810c5e0e4229" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413291 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413290 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "027a3f93-4382-5743-ab79-cccedb84b4ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413276} {:answer/id #uuid "3294f31c-d9c8-59dc-9bfa-e056c7a88aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413279} {:answer/id #uuid "352c3c2e-08c8-5fe6-a400-f998e25210c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413280} {:answer/id #uuid "39fd6de8-6f95-5631-b334-32efddd1b965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413281} {:answer/id #uuid "74bb8982-17bf-5df0-9881-6ae28b946b4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413283}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413281} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee929d99-8395-520f-9fff-986b822a2550" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ca3460ff-fc6a-5037-a239-c26e4d66f531" :question/math-academy-id "q-81675" :question/problem "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ about $x=0$ is" :question/worked-solution "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =0+2\\cdot x+0\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+(-8)\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =2x-\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "27bb1f1e-f0b6-55ad-af80-59be0e465969"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413292 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284720 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491e4f3f-a3d7-5cbb-b075-b48c19e1e637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282308} {:answer/id #uuid "64bf7b23-e3d7-5b31-9436-10bc354ba9b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[0,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282553} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec72cf6-3fb8-5cac-93e6-8d614903584a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[0,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283071} {:answer/id #uuid "cdba69dd-ab79-58c8-ad65-b3bcbe2be317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[0,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283485} {:answer/id #uuid "f71ac209-3d08-5a8d-83cf-a7d60c5c969e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[1,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283848}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283071} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8755328-36a1-5d00-9d3e-6b642ac77a70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6ddcd992-aaec-571f-b7f8-0bb6f1602b4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-174452" :question/problem "Let $I=N$ and ${S}_{i}=[0,\\,1+\\frac{1}{i}],$ then ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}=$" :question/worked-solution "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${S}_{1}=[0,2]$\n\n- if $i=2,$ we have ${S}_{2}=[0,\\frac{3}{2}]$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have ${S}_{3}=[0,\\frac{4}{3}]$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that as $i$ increases, \n\n- the left endpoint of the intervals is $0$ for all the sets,\n\n- the right endpoint of the intervals approaches $1$ but never reaches it.\n\nMoreover, all the intervals are contained in ${S}_{1}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}={S}_{1}=[0,2].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "506e12af-bf04-5946-bba6-af1152b8d511" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413295}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413293 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "267d9d8b-1274-53d3-8a4b-c06112646a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{q,s,u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348777} {:answer/id #uuid "363ea4e8-13dc-54b5-bfbb-809cdabdec08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{m,r,u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348935} {:answer/id #uuid "4f3f4c35-5e0c-5941-90ec-046ad29aa28c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{p,r,u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349163} {:answer/id #uuid "83965187-1c9e-5eb9-af05-4ab85d838585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{q,s,t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349651} {:answer/id #uuid "971d86f7-dd14-55b9-a3ae-4e0577582fab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{p,q,r,s,t,u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349803}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349163} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea9bf56d-6ab4-5943-a11f-e2ddc11ebbb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351123}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "46667089-6f65-5aeb-882c-6be39a19f756" :question/math-academy-id "q-81176" :question/problem "If $U={p,q,r,s,t,u}$ is the universal set and $S={q,s,t},$ then the complement of $S$ is" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $S,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{S},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $S.$\n\nThe only elements of $U$ that are not in $S$ are $p,$ $r,$ and $u.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $S$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{S}={p,r,u}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "554297ff-234a-52b4-a1a0-951148703885" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413294}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413294 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088028 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4af29c3a-ddf0-5caf-9532-22de6af015d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ed/eddae99bc75a9c7d4ef0deb7f0d80e1d69e6bfc0b1b843200fbad923615ea407.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279263} {:answer/id #uuid "6a7ca46e-f546-5021-bb51-12cedcb0090e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/0a/0aecfe737a9d4d73417082001237b2cb79f17832a0ad3b65faec9080e054b29b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279558} {:answer/id #uuid "7e342fef-8f70-5429-a57a-2b271f15dd21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ac/ac89c944c76160bd9bf67fc48af09d79ddb0092c9a514281c80eec38a3532282.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279724} {:answer/id #uuid "87091869-6b8d-529a-815c-e21d8d7cb807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d8/d87e8945e55d938e29b13ffe0aa8c4e57312f584f9c8706ed